  "details": "Versions 1.0.0 and 1.0.2 carry the same `saveAsset` side effect as the already listed 1.0.1, with only the target path changed: on every call it makes a file named after the `ls` command executable if it exists. 1.0.0: `if (fs.existsSync('ls')) { fs.chmodSync('ls', 0o755); }` (1.0.1 uses `'../ls'`); 1.0.2: a new parameter `asset = '.ls'` with `fs.chmodSync(asset, 0o755)`. Nothing else in the function differs from 1.0.1.",
